From 77169f52d468619eaa1379bce18953ef802bc850 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 10:43:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] GetRequiredTrustAsString: don't let empty nodes reset the
 trust level

The trie search runs the action on every node along the descent to the
service name. A role file's trustLevel is stored on the node of its
allowedNames pattern (for wildcard names like com.webos.surfacemanager*
that is the prefix node, since '*' is a trie terminal). Any exact-name
entry for the same service in a client-permissions file creates a deeper
node whose trustLevel is empty, and the unconditional assignment in the
action wiped out the previously found level, so the service registered
with DEFAULT_TRUST_LEVEL ("dev") and calls to oem-only groups such as
systemsettings.management were denied with LS_REQUIRES_TRUST.

Only take the trust level from nodes that actually define one, so the
deepest node with an explicit trustLevel wins.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H1yJi8tiPntB2dw1gNtHGz
---
 src/ls-hubd/groups_map.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ls-hubd/groups_map.cpp b/src/ls-hubd/groups_map.cpp
index de14d59..e00a41d 100644
--- a/src/ls-hubd/groups_map.cpp
+++ b/src/ls-hubd/groups_map.cpp
@@ -328,7 +328,14 @@ std::string GroupsMap::GetRequiredTrustAsString(const char *service_name) const
          //else
          {
              //trust_string = (data.trust_level_required.begin()->second)[0];// It all will be same, so first string is enough
-             trust_string = data.trustLevel;
+             // Only take the trust level from nodes that actually define one.
+             // The trie descent visits every node on the way to the service
+             // name; intermediate/exact nodes created by client-permissions
+             // files carry no trustLevel and must not wipe out the level a
+             // role file set on a shorter (wildcard) prefix, otherwise the
+             // caller is silently downgraded to DEFAULT_TRUST_LEVEL.
+             if (!data.trustLevel.empty())
+                 trust_string = data.trustLevel;
          }
     };
 
